SE: The `logMessage`, `logError`, and `logInfo` methods in the `Logger` class directly concatenate user input into HTML content without sanitation, which may lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities.

BL: 
```
public function logMessage($message) {
    $fp = fopen($this->log_file, 'a');
    fwrite($fp, date("Y-m-d H:i:s") . " - " . $message . "
");
    fclose($fp);
}

public function logError($error) {
    $this->logMessage("Error: " . $error);
}

public function logInfo($message) {
    $this->logMessage("Info: " . $message);
}
```

BUG FOUND: YES
